cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below.
license: Apache-2.0
title: KRYPTARA
abstract: >-
  A research and implementation repository for a governed-change kernel for
  long-lived devices and artefacts: evidence atoms, interval-admitted policy
  tables, a hash-chained authority record, and staged haltable effects.
  Post-quantum migration is one application; the wider "paradigm" named by
  the project title is Speculative and unsupported by evidence (see
  docs/vision-and-scope.md).
authors:
  - family-names: "M R"
    given-names: Kiruthik
    alias: kiruthikpurpose
repository-code: "https://github.com/kiruthikpurpose/KRYPTARA"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
keywords:
  - governed-change kernel
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - evidence-based admission control
  - fault-tolerant authority
  - embedded security
